{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nclaim={\\\"id\\\":\\\"C11-replica-startup-avoids-external-probe\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"concern\\\":\\\"bounded_liveness\\\",\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Constructing a replica must not depend on reaching a fixed external probe address: when that address cannot be dialled, the startup path must still produce a replica (or fail deliberately) instead of dereferencing a failed connection.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"S1-replica-state\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Replica construction on the captured snapshot in an environment where the fixed probe address cannot be dialled: the constructor's inline local-address helper is evaluated as an argument to the latency table.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"the probe address is fixed in the helper rather than taken from configuration\\\",\\\"the constructor evaluates the helper unconditionally, whatever the latency configuration\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"environments where the probe address is reachable\\\",\\\"the latency table's parsing and delay arithmetic\\\",\\\"the rest of replica construction\\\"]},\n \\\"pending\\\":[],\n \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"S1-replica-state\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\"],\n  \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The helper dials a fixed address, discards the error and then closes and dereferences the connection, so a failed dial becomes a nil dereference. The constructor calls the helper inline as an argument, which means every replica construction evaluates it regardless of whether a latency configuration exists; a replica therefore cannot start in an environment without a route to that address.\\\",\n  \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Applies to any deployment or sandbox without connectivity to the probe address, which includes isolated clusters and restricted execution environments.\\\",\n  \\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"whether the probe address is reachable in the deployment the project targets\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}}\nb12={\\\"id\\\":\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\",\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"IP\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":234,\\\"end_line\\\":238,\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Local-address helper: dials a fixed probe address, ignores the error and dereferences the connection.\\\",\n \\\"associations\\\":[{\\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C11-replica-startup-avoids-external-probe\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"S1-replica-state\\\"],\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The helper is the discrepancy and the constructor is where it is evaluated as an argument during startup.\\\"}],\n \\\"pending\\\":[]}\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: in an environment where the fixed probe address cannot be dialled, does the local-address helper return an address or panic? Prefix: the harness calls the helper itself and wraps only that call in recover, so the observation is reported instead of killing the test. Controls: the result prints whether it panicked, the panic value and whether any value was produced; the same call is the one replica construction makes inline.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":claim[\\\"id\\\"],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that calls the implementation's local-address helper and reports whether it returns or panics.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: no replica is constructed; the helper is called directly\\\",\\\"the call is wrapped in recover() to observe a panic; the replica constructor has no recover around it\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[],\\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"S1-replica-state\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The helper is a package-level function with no inputs, so calling it directly exercises exactly what the constructor evaluates.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The execution environment cannot dial the probe address.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"no prerequisite event exists because the helper takes no input; the panic value is the observation\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-probe\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-probe\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"local_address_probe\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event reports whether the helper returned or panicked, which is the duty's observable.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The helper was called once.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-probe\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"local_address_probe\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"panicked\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Resolving the local address must not panic when the probe address is unreachable.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"the check observes the helper rather than a full replica construction, because construction also needs peer addresses and a listener\\\",\\\"whether the project's own deployments always reach the probe address\\\"]}\nq={\\\"audit_spec_version\\\":14,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"ready_for_check\\\",\\\"preferred_check\\\":\\\"direct_test\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"In an environment that cannot reach the fixed probe address, does the helper a replica construction evaluates inline return a local address, or does it discard the dial error and dereference a nil connection so that no replica can be constructed?\\\",\n \\\"importance\\\":\\\"Replica construction evaluates the helper unconditionally, so an unreachable probe address turns into a startup failure for every replica: no process starts, no quorum forms, and the failure is unrelated to any protocol input. The consequence is bounded to environments without a route to that address, which includes isolated or restricted deployments.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"S1-replica-state\\\",\\\"S24-runReplica-epaxos\\\"],\n \\\"contexts\\\":[\\\"probe address unreachable\\\",\\\"helper evaluated as an argument during replica construction\\\"],\n \\\"event_paths\\\":[\\\"the constructor evaluates the helper inline\\\",\\\"the helper dials the probe address and discards the error\\\",\\\"the helper closes and dereferences the connection\\\"],\n \\\"activity_classes\\\":[\\\"A4\\\"],\\\"behavior_ids\\\":[\\\"B15-durable-record\\\"],\\\"fact_ids\\\":[\\\"F7-durable-bytes\\\"],\n \\\"supporting_behavior_ids\\\":{\\\"B15-durable-record\\\":\\\"the construction-time configuration consumer that exists only if the replica is constructed\\\"},\n \\\"obligation_relation_kind\\\":\\\"preservation\\\",\\\"priority\\\":2,\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"scoped to the source: the helper discards the dial error and dereferences the connection, and the constructor evaluates it as an argument, so the call happens before the latency table decides whether a configuration exists (S39-ip-probe, S1-replica-state)\\\",\n   \\\"scoped to the run: the local construction run in this environment reports panicked true with a nil pointer dereference, so the helper cannot return an address here\\\"],\n \\\"unknowns\\\":[\\\"whether the probe address is reachable in the deployments the project uses\\\"],\n \\\"trigger_rationale\\\":\\\"Replica construction is the boundary at which the deployment's configuration becomes a running participant (A4 configuration and eligibility): if the constructor cannot complete without an external route, no participant is eligible at all.\\\"}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"New obligation and its first check for a startup-path defect found while reading the last unread helper: the local-address helper dials a fixed probe address, discards the error and dereferences the connection, and replica construction evaluates it inline, so an environment without a route to that address cannot construct a replica at all. The harness calls the helper directly and observes the nil-pointer panic; the trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review decide the formal outcome. The claim's consequence is bounded to such environments, and the latency table's own parsing is explicitly out of scope.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-ip-probe.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_ip_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{},\n \\\"candidate\\\":{\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The obligation and binding are supplied with the check so the claim exists before the plan references it; the duty is that replica startup must not depend on an external probe.\\\",\\\"action\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"question\\\":q,\\\"obligation\\\":claim,\\\"bindings\\\":[b12]}}\nsrcs=[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"replica/defs/latency.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":234,\\\"end_line\\\":238,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"}]\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-ip-probe.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nsub['sources']=srcs\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-ip-probe.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-ip-probe.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nclaim={\\\"id\\\":\\\"C11-replica-startup-avoids-external-probe\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"concern\\\":\\\"bounded_liveness\\\",\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Constructing a replica must not depend on reaching a fixed external probe address: when that address cannot be dialled, the startup path must still produce a replica (or fail deliberately) instead of dereferencing a failed connection.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"S1-replica-state\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"Replica construction on the captured snapshot in an environment where the fixed probe address cannot be dialled: the constructor's inline local-address helper is evaluated as an argument to the latency table.\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"the probe address is fixed in the helper rather than taken from configuration\\\",\\\"the constructor evaluates the helper unconditionally, whatever the latency configuration\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"environments where the probe address is reachable\\\",\\\"the latency table's parsing and delay arithmetic\\\",\\\"the rest of replica construction\\\"]},\n \\\"pending\\\":[],\n \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"S1-replica-state\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\"],\n  \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The helper dials a fixed address, discards the error and then closes and dereferences the connection, so a failed dial becomes a nil dereference. The constructor calls the helper inline as an argument, which means every replica construction evaluates it regardless of whether a latency configuration exists; a replica therefore cannot start in an environment without a route to that address.\\\",\n  \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Applies to any deployment or sandbox without connectivity to the probe address, which includes isolated clusters and restricted execution environments.\\\",\n  \\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"whether the probe address is reachable in the deployment the project targets\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}}\nb12={\\\"id\\\":\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\",\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"IP\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":234,\\\"end_line\\\":238,\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Local-address helper: dials a fixed probe address, ignores the error and dereferences the connection.\\\",\n \\\"associations\\\":[{\\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C11-replica-startup-avoids-external-probe\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"S1-replica-state\\\"],\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The helper is the discrepancy and the constructor is where it is evaluated as an argument during startup.\\\"}],\n \\\"pending\\\":[]}\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: in an environment where the fixed probe address cannot be dialled, does the local-address helper return an address or panic? Prefix: the harness calls the helper itself and wraps only that call in recover, so the observation is reported instead of killing the test. Controls: the result prints whether it panicked, the panic value and whether any value was produced; the same call is the one replica construction makes inline.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":claim[\\\"id\\\"],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that calls the implementation's local-address helper and reports whether it returns or panics.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: no replica is constructed; the helper is called directly\\\",\\\"the call is wrapped in recover() to observe a panic; the replica constructor has no recover around it\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[],\\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\",\\\"S1-replica-state\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The helper is a package-level function with no inputs, so calling it directly exercises exactly what the constructor evaluates.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The execution environment cannot dial the probe address.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"no prerequisite event exists because the helper takes no input; the panic value is the observation\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-probe\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-probe\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"local_address_probe\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S39-ip-probe\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB12-ip-probe\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event reports whether the helper returned or panicked, which is the duty's observable.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The helper was called once.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-probe\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"local_address_probe\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"panicked\\\",\\\"value\\\":False},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"Resolving the local address must not panic when the probe address is unreachable.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"the check observes the helper rather than a full replica construction, because construction also needs peer addresses and a listener\\\",\\\"whether the project's own deployments always reach the probe address\\\"]}\nq={\\\"audit_spec_version\\\":14,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"ready_for_check\\\",\\\"preferred_check\\\":\\\"direct_test\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"In an environment that cannot reach the fixed probe addre